Short answer: usually yes — use the exact legal name that’s on your Social Security record (the name on your Social Security card or SSA/IRS records) when a form is matching or verifying your SSN. Small differences can cause verification failures or processing delays.

Why:
- Employers, the IRS (TIN/Name Matching), banks, background-check services, and government agencies often verify your SSN against Social Security Administration records. If the name on the form doesn’t match SSA’s record exactly, the check can fail.
